  "releaseNotes": "Adds the ability to enable or disable double-click reporting on Tapo button child devices (S200B and similar). Double-click state was previously read-only: the library surfaced ChildDoubleClickModule.Enabled and a double_click_enabled feature, but exposed no way to change it. KasaDevice.SetChildDoubleClickEnabledAsync (childDeviceId, enabled) and ChildDoubleClickModule.SetEnabledAsync (enabled) now issue the set_double_click_info method over the existing control_child envelope, then refresh parent state so the module reflects the new value. Calling the setter on a child that does not report double-click support throws NotSupportedException before any request is sent; an unknown child identifier continues to throw InvalidOperationException. The console gains a 'child <id|index> doubleclick on|off' action for setting and resetting the option. This release is additive: no existing public API signatures changed.",
